{
 "title": "Solving x² − 5x + 6 = 0",
 "lang": "en",
 "steps": [
  {
   "title": "The Equation & Method 1",
   "say": "We want to solve x squared minus 5x plus 6 equals 0. Our first instinct might be the quadratic formula.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "t_main",
     "x": 80,
     "y": 50,
     "text": "Solve: x² − 5x + 6 = 0",
     "size": 52
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "m1_hdr",
     "x": 80,
     "y": 140,
     "text": "Method 1: Quadratic Formula",
     "size": 38,
     "color": "blue"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "m1_coeff",
     "x": 80,
     "y": 200,
     "text": "a = 1,   b = -5,   c = 6",
     "size": 32,
     "color": "gray"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "m1_form",
     "x": 80,
     "y": 260,
     "text": "x = (-b ± √(b² - 4ac)) / (2a)",
     "size": 34
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Evaluating the Formula",
   "say": "Substituting the coefficients gives 5 plus or minus the square root of 25 minus 24, all divided by 2.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "m1_sub",
     "x": 80,
     "y": 330,
     "text": "x = (5 ± √(25 - 24)) / 2",
     "size": 34
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "m1_disc",
     "x": 80,
     "y": 400,
     "text": "x = (5 ± 1) / 2",
     "size": 34
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "m1_ans",
     "x": 80,
     "y": 470,
     "text": "⇒  x = 3   or   x = 2",
     "size": 36,
     "color": "blue"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Wait—Is There a Simpler Way?",
   "say": "The formula works, but look how much arithmetic we did. Notice the discriminant was a clean square!",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "rect",
     "id": "box_notice",
     "x": 70,
     "y": 550,
     "w": 650,
     "h": 120,
     "color": "red",
     "width": 3
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "t_stop",
     "x": 95,
     "y": 575,
     "text": "Wait: this is overkill!\nThe coefficients are small integers.\nCan we factor directly instead?",
     "size": 28,
     "color": "red"
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "arrow_shift",
     "x1": 740,
     "y1": 340,
     "x2": 850,
     "y2": 340,
     "color": "green",
     "width": 5,
     "arrow": true
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Method 2: Factoring by Inspection",
   "say": "Let's factor directly. We just need two numbers that multiply to positive 6 and add up to negative 5.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "m2_hdr",
     "x": 880,
     "y": 140,
     "text": "Method 2: Factoring (Simpler!)",
     "size": 38,
     "color": "green"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "m2_rule",
     "x": 880,
     "y": 210,
     "text": "Find two numbers p and q such that:",
     "size": 32,
     "color": "ink"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "m2_p_mul",
     "x": 920,
     "y": 270,
     "text": "•  p × q = +6",
     "size": 34,
     "color": "blue"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "m2_p_add",
     "x": 920,
     "y": 330,
     "text": "•  p + q = -5",
     "size": 34,
     "color": "blue"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "m2_pair",
     "x": 880,
     "y": 410,
     "text": "The pair is:  -2  and  -3",
     "size": 36,
     "color": "green"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Instant Solution",
   "say": "Now rewrite the quadratic as (x - 2)(x - 3) = 0. The roots are immediately 2 and 3.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "m2_factor",
     "x": 880,
     "y": 485,
     "text": "(x - 2)(x - 3) = 0",
     "size": 40
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "m2_roots",
     "x": 880,
     "y": 560,
     "text": "⇒  x = 2   or   x = 3",
     "size": 44,
     "color": "green"
    },
    {
     "op": "rect",
     "id": "box_final",
     "x": 860,
     "y": 545,
     "w": 440,
     "h": 75,
     "color": "green",
     "width": 4
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "m2_comp",
     "x": 880,
     "y": 650,
     "text": "Factoring took just one mental step!",
     "size": 30,
     "color": "gray"
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}